-moduledoc """
The Keccak-f[1600] permutation underlying SHA-3, SHAKE, and TurboSHAKE.
This is a low-level primitive for building sponge and duplex
constructions; prefer `m:libsodium_crypto_xof_shake128`,
`m:libsodium_crypto_xof_turboshake128`, or their 256-bit variants for
hashing.

The permutation acts on a 200-byte (1600-bit) state held in an opaque
`t:state/0`. `init/0` returns the all-zero state, `xor_bytes/3` XORs
bytes into it at an offset, `extract_bytes/3` reads bytes from it,
`permute_24/1` applies the full 24-round Keccak-f[1600], and
`permute_12/1` applies the 12-round Keccak-p[1600,12] used by
TurboSHAKE. Offsets and lengths must satisfy `Offset + Length =< 200`.

States are immutable values: every operation returns a new state and
leaves its argument unchanged.

```erlang
State0 = libsodium_crypto_core_keccak1600:init(),
State1 = libsodium_crypto_core_keccak1600:xor_bytes(State0, <<"abc", 16#1F>>, 0),
State2 = libsodium_crypto_core_keccak1600:xor_bytes(State1, <<16#80>>, 167),
State3 = libsodium_crypto_core_keccak1600:permute_24(State2),
Out = libsodium_crypto_core_keccak1600:extract_bytes(State3, 0, 32),
Out = crypto:hash_xof(shake128, <<"abc">>, 256).
```
""".
